 href=\"./Init/Data/SInt/Basic.html#Int64\">Int64</a> → <a href=\"./Init/Data/SInt/Basic.html#Int64\">Int64</a> → <a href=\"./MPN/WordGcd.html#MPN.LeadWords\">MPN.LeadWords</a></span></div></div>","info":{"doc":"","docLink":"./MPN/WordGcd.html#MPN.LeadWords.mk","kind":"ctor","line":67,"name":"MPN.LeadWords.mk","sourceLink":"https://github.com/fgdorais/lean4-mpn/blob/862f63d87fc6e56d648eb33296f1cf7ff688fd89/MPN/WordGcd.lean#L67-L70"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">structure</span><span class=\"decl_name\"> <a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./MPN/WordGcd.html#MPN.LeadWords\"><span class=\"name\">MPN</span>.<span class=\"name\">LeadWords</span></a> </span><span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><a href=\"./foundational_types.html\">Type</a></div></div>","info":{"doc":"Two words, as one object with unboxed fields.","docLink":"./MPN/WordGcd.html#MPN.LeadWords","kind":"structure","line":67,"name":"MPN.LeadWords","sourceLink":"https://github.com/fgdorais/lean4-mpn/blob/862f63d87fc6e56d648eb33296f1cf7ff688fd89/MPN/WordGcd.lean#L67-L70"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">def</span><span class=\"decl_name\"> <a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./MPN/WordGcd.html#MPN.lehmerSteps\"><span class=\"name\">MPN</span>.<span class=\"name\">lehmerSteps</span></a> </span><span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">x </span><span class=\"fn\">y </span><span class=\"fn\">A </span><span class=\"fn\">B </span><span class=\"fn\">C </span><span class=\"fn\">D</span> : <a href=\"./Init/Data/SInt/Basic.html#Int64\">Int64</a>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Nat\">Nat</a> → <a href=\"./MPN/WordGcd.html#MPN.Cofactors\">Cofactors</a></span></div></div>","info":{"doc":"Euclid's algorithm on the leading words `x ≥ y` of two numbers, with the cofactors `A`, `B`, `C`,\n`D` of the steps so far, like GMP's `hgcd2` on one word: it stops when the remainder falls below\n`2³¹`, half the bits of the words, which keeps the cofactors below `2³¹`, or when Jebelean's\ncondition fails, which makes the quotients those of the full numbers. A quotient of `1`, the most\ncommon, costs a comparison rather than a division. It computes in `Int64`, since `Int` boxes\nvalues from `2³¹`. Nothing is proved about it: the caller checks the cofactors it returns, and\ntakes a step of Euclid's algorithm when they do not apply.","docLink":"./MPN/WordGcd.html#MPN.lehmerSteps","kind":"def","line":42,"name":"MPN.lehmerSteps","sourceLink":"https://github.com/fgdorais/lean4-mpn/blob/862f63d87fc6e56d648eb33296f1cf7ff688fd89/MPN/WordGcd.lean#L42-L65"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">abbrev</span><span class=\"decl_name\"> <a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./MPN/WordGcd.html#MPN.Cofactors.D\"><span class=\"name\">MPN</span>.<span class=\"name\">Cofactors</span>.<span class=\"name\">D</span></a> </span><span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">self</span> : <a href=\"./MPN/WordGcd.html#MPN.Cofactors\">Cofactors</a>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><a href=\"./Init/Data/SInt/Basic.html#Int64\">Int64</a></div></div>","info":{"doc":"","docLink":"./MPN/WordGcd.html#MPN.Cofactors.D","kind":"def","line":40,"name":"MPN.Cofactors.D","sourceLink":"https://github.com/fgdorais/lean4-mpn/blob/862f63d87fc6e56d648eb33296f1cf7ff688fd89/MPN/WordGcd.lean#L40-L40"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">abbrev</span><span class=\"decl_name\"> <a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./MPN/WordGcd.html#MPN.Cofactors.C\"><span class=\"name\">MPN</span>.<span class=\"name\">Cofactors</span>.<span class=\"name\">C</span></a> </span><span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">self</span> : <a href=\"./MPN/WordGcd.html#MPN.Cofactors\">Cofactors</a>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><d